          "reasoning": "On app-01, user ubuntu ran 'sudo ./stdout_etc.sh' (proc-8d6f05d903). The script, running as root under /bin/dash (proc-515c01cf7c), started three cat processes that read /etc/shadow, /etc/passwd and /etc/sudoers. It redirected their output into world-accessible copies in the home directory: /home/ubuntu/file_shadow, file_passwd and file_sudoers. This matches OS credential dumping (T1003.008): password hashes and privilege configuration were staged in a user-writable location. No administrative or backup context was found to explain it. Response: isolate the host, rotate the ubuntu and root credentials (the shadow hashes are exposed), and delete the dumped files.",
